---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="OSINT Scanner"
	eyebrow="[ 04 · RECON ]"
	description="Map a deployed contract’s attack surface from WASM alone — no source, no ABI file, no cooperation from the author."
>
	<h2>What it does</h2>
	<p>Given only a Contract ID, the scanner:</p>
	<ol>
		<li>
			Fetches WASM via read-only RPC (<code>getContractWasmByContractId</code>) — nothing
			broadcast.
		</li>
		<li>Decodes the <code>contractspecv0</code> custom section from the binary.</li>
		<li>Builds a registry of user-defined types (structs, unions, enums).</li>
		<li>Renders every function: name, parameter types, return presence.</li>
	</ol>

	<h2>Domain objects</h2>
	<pre><code>ScanResult &#123;
  contractId: string
  bytecodeSize: number
  functions: ScannedFunction[]   // name, params[], hasReturn
  udtRegistry: UdtRegistry       // Map of UDT definitions
&#125;

ScanError codes:
  CONTRACT_NOT_FOUND | XDR_ALIGN_FAILURE | RPC_UNAVAILABLE | UNKNOWN</code></pre>

	<p>
		<code>ScanError.code</code> is the stable switch both TUI and CLI use — presentation
		layers must not parse <code>message</code> text to decide what happened.
	</p>

	<h2>Parsing notes</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<code>parseContractSpecSection()</code> is a pure, network-free step — unit-testable
			with synthetic XDR buffers.
		</li>
		<li>
			Alignment-tolerant decode: the parser brute-forces 4-byte aligned lengths until an
			<code>ScSpecEntry</code> parses, then advances.
		</li>
		<li>
			UDT resolution used later by Chaos Monkey has depth limits and cycle detection; unknown
			types cause generators to skip rather than invent values.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<Callout type="tip" title="Paid HTTP surface">
		<p>
			<code>kuyfi-server</code> exposes only this read-only scanner over
			<code>GET /scan/:contractId</code> (x402). Chaos Monkey is never offered over HTTP
			because it broadcasts transactions.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2>TUI</h2>
	<p>
		Home → <strong>[1] OSINT Scanner</strong>. Paste a Contract ID, watch the fetch, inspect
		the attack-surface table. The last successful scan can feed Chaos Monkey in the same
		session.
	</p>
</DocsLayout>
